'''''Lophocolea bidentata''''' is a species of [[liverwort]] belonging to the family [[Lophocoleaceae]].<ref name="GBIF">{{cite web |title=''Lophocolea bidentata'' (L.) Dumort.|url=https://www.gbif.org/species/4276916 |website=www.gbif.org |access-date=5 May 2022 |language=en}}</ref>

A study in tropical [[Ecuador]] found that ''Lophocolea bidentata'' was typically not found in urban environments despite being found in a nearby pristine location, suggesting that the species is sensitive to [[anthropogenic effects]] such as the presence of [[wastewater]] and [[heavy metal pollution]].<ref Name="CV2019">{{cite journal |last1=Vásquez |first1=Cristina |last2=Calva |first2=James |last3=Morocho |first3=Ramiro |last4=Donoso |first4=David A. |last5=Benítez |first5=Ángel |date=2019 |title=Bryophyte Communities along a Tropical Urban River Respond to Heavy Metal and Arsenic Pollution |journal=Water |volume=11 |issue=4 |pages=813|doi=10.3390/w11040813 |doi-access=free }}</ref>

